WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.896 --> 00:00:02.681
[Waves crashing]

00:00:02.681 --> 00:00:04.332
[Gulls cawing]

00:00:04.332 --> 00:00:07.320
♪♪♪

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.920
- Now, I'm at the point where

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.823
the work is gonna show.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.603
I feel like I put a lotta hours in.

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.296
I sacrificed a lotta stuff, so.

00:00:25.296 --> 00:00:27.650
[Crowd cheering]

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.062
If you don't believe in
yourself, then who really will?

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:30.895
- Gimme three!

00:00:30.895 --> 00:00:31.728
- [Clapping]

00:00:31.728 --> 00:00:32.969
- Gimme two! Gimme one!

00:00:32.969 --> 00:00:34.840
♪♪♪

00:00:39.315 --> 00:00:42.148
One, two, three!
- [In unison:] Boom!

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.297
[Whistle blowing]

00:01:04.907 --> 00:01:05.740
- OK. What's up?

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:07.840
I'm Simeon Wilcher, class of 2023.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.620
I'm a University of North Carolina commit.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.453
- [Offscreen:] All right, perfect.

00:01:11.453 --> 00:01:12.303
Thank you.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.473
- Growin' up, I wasn't
really, I wasn't really a basketball player.

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:21.600
I started really takin'
basketball serious

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.323
at around, like, seven, eight years old.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.570
Like, just bein' around,
watchin' everybody play

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:30.520
and goin' to high school games.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.150
Me and my pops would travel.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:34.060
Me and my pops, my brother, my mom.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.820
So that just helped, like,
grow my love for it.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:39.370
And then over the years, watchin' players,

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.655
my love is growin' by the day.

00:01:41.655 --> 00:01:42.741
[Buzzer sounding]

00:01:42.741 --> 00:01:43.574
♪♪♪

00:01:43.574 --> 00:01:47.088
Sometimes I catch myself watchin'
highlight reels of myself.

00:01:47.088 --> 00:01:50.083
[Crowd cheering]

00:01:50.083 --> 00:01:52.500
- [Announcer:] Simeon Wilcher!

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.510
- Like, that's what I used to do.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:59.557
Man, I used to go on YouTube
and just watch players hoop.

00:01:59.557 --> 00:02:00.513
And so now it's just like,

00:02:00.513 --> 00:02:02.200
it's kinda crazy to me

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.950
that I know somewhere out there

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.170
that somebody's actually
searchin' my name up

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:08.273
on Google and watchin' me play.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.140
As a hooper, you really
motivate people to keep goin'.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:17.990
So knowin' that I could actually help

00:02:19.128 --> 00:02:20.680
somebody, somebody out there get through whatever

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.753
they're goin' through means a lot.

00:02:23.608 --> 00:02:26.275
[Buzzer sounding]

00:02:27.228 --> 00:02:32.228
- [Announcer:] Simeon Wilcher,
for three!

00:02:38.493 --> 00:02:41.493
[Players talking]

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.213
- [Simeon:] Puttin' on the
jersey for Roselle means a lot.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.360
Knowin' that the recent
history in the last 10 years,

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.330
that Roselle's won three ToCs,

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.660
like, that means a lot.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:01.938
Not everybody is blessed
with the opportunity.

00:03:01.938 --> 00:03:04.323
[Players clapping]

00:03:04.323 --> 00:03:06.477
- Gimme one!
- [Clapping]
- Gimme two!
- [Clapping]

00:03:06.477 --> 00:03:08.884
- Gimme two!
- [Clapping]
- Gimme three!
- [Clapping]

00:03:08.884 --> 00:03:12.301
- One, one, one! When I
say three, you say four!

00:03:12.301 --> 00:03:13.384
One, two, three!

00:03:13.384 --> 00:03:14.858
- [In unison:] Boom!

00:03:14.858 --> 00:03:15.691
♪♪♪

00:03:15.691 --> 00:03:19.460
- Freshman year, I was the
little brother to everybody.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.110
Yeah, really all of my older brothers

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:22.110
on the team with me.

00:03:23.078 --> 00:03:24.380
I always played with a chip on my shoulder

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:27.400
because some people, like, just tossed me

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:30.600
to the side a little bit, and
I don't really like that.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:34.170
And also I feed off, like, my older brother.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:35.910
But he didn't really get to shine

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:37.870
that I feel like he deserved.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:40.750
So that just adds to
the chip on my shoulder.

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:42.553
I feel like I'm doin' it for him too.

00:03:44.934 --> 00:04:07.517
♪♪♪

00:04:08.761 --> 00:04:11.678
[Players clapping]

00:04:22.574 --> 00:04:23.407
- And we know we can beat people

00:04:23.407 --> 00:04:24.630
when we play our best, OK?

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:27.030
Today was a good game
against a good national team

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:28.770
with a couple of really good players.

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:30.680
Didn't have our A-game,
still found a way to win

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.200
by doin' the things that we needed to do.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.274
All right? Congratulations.

00:04:33.274 --> 00:04:34.107
Good win. Bring it in.

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:36.690
[Players clapping]

00:04:38.465 --> 00:04:40.410
- What I want for my future
involving basketball,

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:41.990
I want it to take me to the NBA.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:45.060
Not only just to be a
player and just get drafted.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:47.230
I wanna be a superstar

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.280
and be a role model for the younger kids.

00:04:52.827 --> 00:04:53.727
I love basketball.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:56.920
I love basketball, and my
love is just gonna grow

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:57.870
as the years go on.

